From c26d00ae5b223ed786f5fa60bf660c62e48ef036 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:45:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] drm/tests: add KUnit tests for DisplayID 2.0 luminance
 parsing

Add KUnit tests for the luminance range that the DRM core takes from
the DisplayID 2.0 Display Parameters data block. They build EDIDs with a
DisplayID 2.0 extension block and run them through
drm_edid_connector_update(), so the production parser is exercised
rather than a second copy of the decoder, and then check
display_info.luminance_range and display_info.hdr_sink_metadata.

The cases cover:

 - the full coverage maximum versus the 10 percent coverage peak, a
   tiny valid, a zero and a subnormal minimum, rounding at the
   whole-nit boundaries, negative, infinite, NaN and -0 encodings, and
   the ordering of minimum and maximum both as encoded and after
   rounding;

 - every revision byte and Luminance Information value, and payload
   lengths from 0 to 31;

 - the first of two Display Parameters blocks being the one used, and
   the range being reset by an EDID without one and by no EDID at all;

 - CTA HDR static metadata taking precedence, with and without a mapped
   luminance range and with the DisplayID and CTA extensions in either
   order, with the HDR sink metadata left exactly as the CTA block
   describes it. A CTA block without a mapped range may use the
   validated DisplayID limits.

A DisplayID-only EDID must leave hdr_sink_metadata zeroed; that is
checked after every update.

The tests and this changelog were drafted with AI coding assistants
(OpenAI Codex, then reviewed and reworked with Anthropic Claude through
Claude Code). Human review remains with the submitter.

---
